      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬(¬P⇒Q).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(¬P⇒Q)≡¬(¬(¬P)∨Q).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬(¬P)∨Q)≡¬(P∨Q).\n$$\n\nFinally, we can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(P∨Q)≡¬P∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $¬P∧¬Q.$",
